---
import BaseLayout from "~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "~/lib/site";

const updated = "19 October 2026";
const contact = site.emails.projects;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy | NSQD"
  description="How NSQD handles the details you send through nsqd.co: what the contact form collects, where it goes, how long we keep it, and how to ask for deletion."
  pathname="/privacy/"
>
  <section class="section border-b border-edge">
    <div class="wrap max-w-3xl">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 font-sans font-extrabold tracking-tightest text-paper leading-[0.95] text-[clamp(2.5rem,6vw,5rem)]">
        Privacy policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-7 text-paper/85 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        Short version: we collect what you give us through the contact form, we
        use it to reply, and we don't sell it or pass it on. The detail is below.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-12 space-y-10 text-paper/85 leading-relaxed">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-paper">Who we are</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Necessity Squared (NSQD) is the data controller for nsqd.co. We work
            out of Jebel Ali, Dubai, United Arab Emirates and Wynberg, Cape Town,
            South Africa. Questions about this policy go to
            <a href={`mailto:${contact}`} class="text-sun hover:underline">{contact}</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-paper">What the contact form collects</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Your name, email address, phone number with its country code, the
            subject you pick, and your message. Name, email, subject and message
            are required. The form also has a hidden field that only bots fill
            in, which we use to drop spam before it reaches us.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-paper">Where it goes</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Each submission is emailed to NSQD staff through Resend, our email
            delivery provider, and lands in our inbox. The site itself keeps no
            database of submissions. Resend handles the message only to deliver
            it, under its own privacy policy.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-paper">Why we use it and how long we keep it</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We use your details to reply to you and, if the enquiry turns into a
            job, to run that job. We keep the email while the enquiry or project
            is live, then for as long as normal business records require. If you
            want it gone sooner, ask and we'll delete it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-paper">Analytics</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We use Plausible Analytics. It is cookieless, does not follow you
            across other sites and collects no personal data. We see page counts,
            referrers and rough country, nothing that identifies you.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-paper">WhatsApp</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The WhatsApp buttons on this site open a chat with us inside
            WhatsApp. From that point the conversation runs under Meta's terms
            and WhatsApp's privacy policy, not this one.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-paper">Cookies</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">The site sets no tracking cookies.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-paper">Your rights</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            This policy is written for UAE data protection law and South Africa's
            Protection of Personal Information Act (POPIA). You can ask what we
            hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it. Email
            <a href={`mailto:${contact}`} class="text-sun hover:underline">{contact}</a>
            and we'll confirm within 30 days. In South Africa you can also raise
            a complaint with the Information Regulator.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-paper">Changes</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            If this page changes, the date below changes with it.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 font-spec text-sm text-mute">Last updated: {updated}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
